    "title": "pandas.DatetimeTZDtype.unit — pandas 3.1.0.dev0 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.DatetimeTZDtype.unit#\n\n- property DatetimeTZDtype.unit[source]#\n- The precision of the datetime data. Returns the time resolution as one of `'s'` ,`'ms'` ,`'us'` ,\nor`'ns'` .See also \n  - `DatetimeTZDtype.tz`\n  - Retrieves the timezone.\n Examples >>> from zoneinfo import ZoneInfo >>> dtype = pd.DatetimeTZDtype(tz=ZoneInfo(\"America/Los_Angeles\")) >>> dtype.unit 'ns'",
